I don't believe there is such a thing as a "legit" or "not-ligit"
ascension.  It's a game.  Do whatever you want, and have fun.  When I
started playing, I savescummed unabashedly.  It's a great way to
learn.  Some people will call it "cheating".  It's my computer, time,
and entertainment, and they're rules don't apply.

HOWEVER!  If you post your results to a community for open discussion,
you should be prepared to defend your choices!  Some people may
disagree with your choices, and you can choose to take those
disagreements to heart or not.  (Has anyone ever posted a YAFAP that
included save-scumming?  I'd love to read that thread!)

I think it's pretty clear that saving a file to protect it from a
crash isn't save-scumming.

A more interesting scenario, though, is if you save your file, then
play for a while and find yourself in a really sticky situation
(likely going to die, but maybe could escape).  At that point, your
computer crashes and you lose your game.  Do you restore your save
file or not?  If you ascend, what does that mean?  In my opinion, the
only meaningful answers to these questions can only come from you.

